def largest_fall(prices):
    worst = 0
    if len(prices) > 0:
        peak = prices[0]
        for p in prices:
            if p > peak:
                peak = p
            if peak - p > worst:
                worst = peak - p
    return worst

explain.text:
The loop keeps the running peak and, at each price, the gap `peak - p`. The answer is the largest gap seen. One pass is enough, because the peak only ever looks backwards.

